---Cancel a deployment
---
---Cancels a deployment that is currently in progress, stopping the build before it completes. Use this to recover quickly from accidental deploys, wrong-branch pushes, or builds with known errors — without waiting for them to finish. Returns 400 if the deployment is no longer cancelable (already `READY`, `ERROR`, or `CANCELED`). Returns the updated deployment object with `readyState: 'CANCELED'` on success.
---
---`PATCH /v12/deployments/{id}/cancel`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.CancelDeploymentRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.CancelDeploymentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_deployment(input) end

---Create a new deployment
---
---Creates a new deployment for the authenticated team or user. For non-git deployments, upload files first via the file upload API, then reference them here by SHA — or inline small files directly in the request body. To redeploy an existing deployment, provide its `deploymentId`; all settings are inherited unless explicitly overridden. The deployment begins building immediately and transitions through `QUEUED` → `INITIALIZING` → `BUILDING` before reaching `READY` or `ERROR`.
---
---`POST /v13/deployments`
---Errors: BadRequest, PaymentRequired, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.deployments.CreateDeploymentRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.CreateDeploymentResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_deployment(input) end

---Delete a Deployment
---
---This API allows you to delete a deployment, either by supplying its `id` in the URL or the `url` of the deployment as a query parameter. You can obtain the ID, for example, by listing all deployments.
---
---`DELETE /v13/deployments/{id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.deployments.DeleteDeploymentRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.DeleteDeploymentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_deployment(input) end

---Get a deployment by ID or URL
---
---Retrieves information for a deployment either by supplying its ID (`id` property) or Hostname (`url` property). Additional details will be included when the authenticated user or team is an owner of the deployment.
---
---`GET /v13/deployments/{idOrUrl}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_deployment(input) end

---Get deployment events
---
---Get the build logs of a deployment by deployment ID and build ID. It can work as an infinite stream of logs or as a JSON endpoint depending on the input parameters.
---
---`GET /v3/deployments/{idOrUrl}/events`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentEventsRequest
---@return (vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentEventsResponseBodyList|distilled.Null)? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_deployment_events(input) end

---Get Deployment File Contents
---
---Allows to retrieve the content of a file by supplying the file identifier and the deployment unique identifier. The response body will contain a JSON response containing the contents of the file encoded as base64.
---
---`GET /v8/deployments/{id}/files/{fileId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentFileContentsRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentFileContentsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_deployment_file_contents(input) end

---List deployments
---
---List deployments under the authenticated user or team. If a deployment hasn't finished uploading (is incomplete), the `url` property will have a value of `null`.
---
---`GET /v7/deployments`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input? vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentsRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.GetDeploymentsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_deployments(input) end

---List Deployment Files
---
---Allows to retrieve the file structure of the source code of a deployment by supplying the deployment unique identifier. If the deployment was created with the Vercel CLI or the API directly with the `files` key, it will have a file tree that can be retrievable.
---
---`GET /v6/deployments/{id}/files`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.ListDeploymentFilesRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.ListDeploymentFilesResponseBodyList? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_deployment_files(input) end

---Update deployment integration action
---
---Updates the deployment integration action for the specified integration installation
---
---`PATCH /v1/deployments/{deploymentId}/integrations/{integrationConfigurationId}/resources/{resourceId}/actions/{action}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.deployments.UpdateIntegrationDeploymentActionRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.UpdateIntegrationDeploymentActionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_integration_deployment_action(input) end

---Upload Deployment Files
---
---Before you create a deployment you need to upload the required files for that deployment. To do it, you need to first upload each file to this endpoint. Once that's completed, you can create a new deployment with the uploaded files. The file content must be placed inside the body of the request. In the case of a successful response you'll receive a status code 200 with an empty body.
---
---`POST /v2/files`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input? vercel.deployments.UploadFileRequest
---@return vercel.deployments.UploadFileResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:upload_file(input) end

